		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=30695#p30695"><![CDATA[
Hello,<br><br>Looking at a number of physics engines it seems that some use an explicit box-box collider, while others use GJK. Bullet appears to support both, with the Box v Box from ODE being used as default.<br><br>What are the pros and cons of these two approaches? Is there any documentation or description of the technique ODE uses - it appears to be SAT? Our engine supports persistent manifolds, so I would assume GJK and Box v Box would ultimately generate the same point set.<br><br>Has anyone experimented with exploiting frame coherence with either of these approaches?<br><br>I would like to implement an effective and robust solution so input and experiences would be appreciated.<br><br>Best,<br><br>S<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=10211">sphet</a> — Sun May 12, 2013 7:21 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
